<code>assert !\old(this.isEmpty()) => \result.compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0;</code>

However, since `PriorityQueue` does not have an `isEmpty()` method, we can use `size()` instead:

<code>assert \old(this.size()) > 0 => \result.compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0;</code>

This ensures that if the queue was not empty before the `poll()` operation, the element returned (`\result`) is greater than or equal to the element that was previously at the head of the queue (`\old(this.peek())`).
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.size()) > 0 => this.peek().compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0;</code>

This assert statement checks that if the queue is not empty before the `poll` operation, the element at the head of the queue after the operation is greater than or equal to the element that was at the head before the operation. Note that since `peek()` returns the head of the queue, we use it to compare the elements before and after the `poll` operation. The `compareTo` method is used to compare the elements based on their natural ordering or the comparator provided.
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(this.isEmpty()) => \result.compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0;</code>
